  "instructions": {
    "en": "On each trial two letter strings appear, one directly above the other. Decide whether *both* strings are real English words.\n\nIf both are real words, press \"Yes\" (key J).\nIf either one (or both) is not a real word, press \"No\" (key F).\n\nYour response ends the display, so answer as quickly as you can while staying accurate. Each trial starts with the warning word READY followed by a fixation box.\n\nA short practice block with feedback comes first.",
    "he": "בכל ניסיון יוצגו שתי מחרוזות אותיות, אחת מעל השנייה. עליך להחליט האם *שתי* המחרוזות הן מילים אמיתיות באנגלית.\n\nאם שתי המחרוזות הן מילים – לחץ/י על \"כן\" (מקש J).\nאם אחת מהן (או שתיהן) אינה מילה אמיתית – לחץ/י על \"לא\" (מקש F).\n\nהתגובה מסיימת את הצגת הגירוי, לכן השתדל/י להגיב מהר ככל האפשר אך גם בדיוק מרבי. לפני כל ניסיון תופיע המילה READY ולאחריה ריבוע קיבוע.\n\nתחילה יוצג תרגול קצר עם משוב."
  },
  "simplifications": [
    {
      "why": "The original normed word lists are not reproduced in the paper; crossing pair type with 15 item slots keeps the design fully text-based with no assets.",
      "what": "Stimulus items are a curated illustrative set (associated pairs, recombined unassociated pairs, and word/nonword combinations) rather than the paper's association-norm-derived items."
    },
    {
      "why": "The derived-factor mapping must be complete, while the exclusions yield exactly 10 trials in each of the five pair types = 50 test trials, the length requested by the lecturer.",
      "what": "The item mapping defines strings for all 5 x 15 = 75 pairType x slot cells, but slots 11–15 of every condition are excluded from the trial list, and the paper's unequal condition proportions are replaced by an equal 10-per-type design."
    },
    {
      "why": "The runtime's response phase waits for input rather than timing out. Students typically respond in ~1 s, so removing the cutoff affects only a handful of very slow trials.",
      "what": "No 3000 ms response deadline; the stimulus stays on screen until the participant responds."
    },
    {
      "why": "Feedback content depends on the response, which a timed display phase cannot express; practice feedback suffices for learning the mapping, and omitting test feedback avoids strategic slowing.",
      "what": "Trial-by-trial accuracy feedback is given in the practice block only (11 trials), not in the 50 test trials."
    },
    {
      "why": "The renderer shuffles the crossed trial list; with 50 trials over 5 types, occasional runs of the same type have a negligible effect on condition means.",
      "what": "Trial order is fully randomized with no constraint on consecutive repeats of the same pair type."
    },
    {
      "why": "The paper reports a brief warning signal without specifying its duration; 500 ms is a standard value and was confirmed by the lecturer.",
      "what": "The 'READY' warning signal is fixed at 500 ms."
    },
    {
      "why": "Requested by the lecturer to keep the response display minimal and uncluttered during the timed task.",
      "what": "Response buttons are labelled only \"כן\" / \"לא\" (\"Yes\" / \"No\"), with the full decision rule stated in the instructions instead of on the buttons."
    },
    {
      "why": "Requested by the lecturer, who asked for a different typeface for the stimuli; letter-string legibility is unaffected.",
      "what": "The two letter strings are displayed in a sans-serif typeface rather than monospace (the READY warning remains monospace)."
    }
  ]
}
